WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.210
Week 22: Double Pronouns, Se, and Reference. report accidental events give concise instructions maintain reference across sentences

2
00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:17.716
Form and meaning. Double-object order; le/les to se; redundant indirect objects; accidental se; discourse reference.

3
00:00:17.716 --> 00:00:42.971
Model set. Se me perdieron las llaves. El informe se lo mandé a Clara. A ellos se les olvidó la cita. Explícaselo antes de la reunión. No se nos cayó el equipo; falló el soporte. I lost my keys. I sent the report to Clara. They forgot the appointment. Explain it to him or her before the meeting. We did not drop the equipment; the support failed.

4
00:00:42.971 --> 00:00:53.123
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:00:53.123 --> 00:01:06.687
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: report accidental events; give concise instructions; maintain reference across sentences. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:06.687 --> 00:01:32.817
Model language. Se me perdieron las llaves. — I lost my keys. El informe se lo mandé a Clara. — I sent the report to Clara. A ellos se les olvidó la cita. — They forgot the appointment. Explícaselo antes de la reunión. — Explain it to him or her before the meeting. No se nos cayó el equipo; falló el soporte. — We did not drop the equipment; the support failed.

7
00:01:32.817 --> 00:01:42.715
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
